Hina glanced at Curtis, then away. “I can walk you. It’s close.”
Curtis nodded. He picked up the water, finished it, and stood. The explanation sat clear. The rules sat clearer. He still didn’t have a name for the quiet pull that had followed him through the whole shift, and he still wasn’t looking for one.
