Curtis paused, duffel already on his shoulder. The club lights were low behind them. “Who knows. There’s no rule that says I can’t do both later.” His accent stayed even. “I ain’t a business expert. But I’m sure a lot of people would pay decent money to sit with a top hero for an hour. That’s what I’m aiming to be.”
